From: Halhadus <eneshakan45@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: simple: match the Exynos7870 CSIS receiver

Use the existing supported-device entry from Alessandro Fontana's
android_external_libcamera commit 95f6b20d917be23759710c1f85a6f2deab106e0a.
The boolean enables software ISP. This does not fix sensor probing or
replace the PipeWire SPA plugin. Prepared against Debian libcamera 0.4.0.

Signed-off-by: Halhadus <eneshakan45@proton.me>
---
diff --git a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
@@ -200,6 +200,7 @@
 
 static const SimplePipelineInfo supportedDevices[] = {
 	{ "dcmipp", {}, false },
+	{ "exynos7870-csis", {}, true },
 	{ "imx7-csi", { { "pxp", 1 } }, false },
 	{ "intel-ipu6", {}, true },
 	{ "j721e-csi2rx", {}, true },
